From 7610b2454e9dcde83eaf55566746e1d59361696d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:01:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/33] perf(sha256): x86 SHA extensions and streaming input
 for native sha256

sha256() compresses complete blocks straight from the input instead of first
copying it byte by byte, and pads only the tail. Block compression uses the
x86 SHA extensions (SHA256RNDS2/MSG1/MSG2) when CPUID reports them, falling
back to the portable sha256_block. 4 MiB: 19.2 ms -> 2.6 ms (SHA-NI), 14.3 ms
portable. Used by the Grumpkin CRS integrity check on every load.
